nai Peninsula of Egypt. Located at the foot of Mount Sinai, it was built between 548 and 565, and is the world's oldest continuously inhabited Christian monastery.", "newValue": "Saint Catherine's Monastery, officially known as the Sacred Autonomous Royal Monastery of Saint Catherine of the Holy and God-Trodden Mount Sinai, stands as a testament to early Christian monasticism. Established between 548 and 565 CE at the foot of Mount Sinai in present-day Egypt, it is recognized as the oldest continuously inhabited Christian monastery in the world. Its strategic location has made it a vital site for pilgrimage and scholarship, drawing numerous visitors over the centuries, including Byzantine emperors and scholars from various cultures. The monastery's significance extends beyond its religious role, serving as a beacon of cultural exchange and preservation throughout the tumultuous eras of history.

